WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Why can oysters live in the lower James River but not near Richmond?

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.540
Follow one Virginia landscape from mountain forest to salty Bay, and look for both

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.760
kinds of clues. Some clues are alive.

4
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.640
Others are parts of the surroundings.

5
00:00:20.283 --> 00:00:25.523
An ecosystem includes all living things in a place and their nonliving surroundings.

6
00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:32.023
The living side includes plants, animals, fungi, microorganisms, and their

7
00:00:32.023 --> 00:00:37.703
interactions. Watch a deer eat acorns while fungi spread through a fallen log.

8
00:00:39.023 --> 00:00:41.163
These relationships are biotic factors.

9
00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:47.567
The nonliving side includes climate, sunlight, water, soil, air, and nutrients.

10
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:50.487
These are abiotic factors.

11
00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:55.467
Rain darkens the soil while sunlight shifts under the tree canopy.

12
00:00:56.907 --> 00:01:00.667
Both sides share one place, and changes on either side can matter.

13
00:01:01.717 --> 00:01:06.037
Now the forest canopy grows thicker, but everything else stays the same.

14
00:01:07.437 --> 00:01:09.197
Less sunlight reaches the forest floor.

15
00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:13.097
What do you predict will happen to the small plants below?

16
00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:22.843
The shaded plants grow poorly or disappear from the picture.

17
00:01:24.323 --> 00:01:27.463
Light is one condition that can limit where plants survive.

18
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:30.923
Deep or muddy water can block light too.

19
00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:35.923
That helps explain why few plants grow on some underwater floors.

20
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:41.853
Climate is the usual pattern of temperature and rainfall over many years.

21
00:01:43.193 --> 00:01:48.053
Earth's tilt changes sunlight angle and day length as Earth travels around the sun.

22
00:01:49.553 --> 00:01:53.953
Latitude, elevation, land shape, and human actions also shape climate.

23
00:01:55.653 --> 00:01:57.293
Climate is part of the abiotic side.

24
00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:00.713
Carry the same paired view across Virginia.

25
00:02:02.113 --> 00:02:04.933
A forest is a terrestrial ecosystem on land.

26
00:02:06.193 --> 00:02:09.193
A mountain stream is freshwater, with very little salt.

27
00:02:10.813 --> 00:02:12.473
Ocean water is marine and salty.

28
00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:18.553
Between them, an estuary mixes fresh river water with salty ocean water.

29
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:23.223
These labels describe surroundings, not empty containers.

30
00:02:24.683 --> 00:02:29.723
Organisms must handle those conditions while also finding food and meeting other

31
00:02:29.723 --> 00:02:36.103
living things. Living interactions and nonliving conditions help decide what can

32
00:02:36.103 --> 00:02:41.943
live where. That rule may explain the oyster puzzle, but we need evidence along the

33
00:02:41.943 --> 00:02:42.923
river.

34
00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.707
No single factor tells the whole story.

35
00:02:46.907 --> 00:02:50.627
A suitable condition does not prove an organism was present.

36
00:02:51.907 --> 00:02:54.647
A range match is a clue, not a complete answer.

37
00:02:56.087 --> 00:03:00.687
Ecosystems also change as conditions, populations, and species change.

38
00:03:01.827 --> 00:03:05.047
The next step is to test one condition along the James.
